# Shell scripts must use LF so Docker/Linux entrypoints work on Windows checkouts.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Line endings: store as LF in git, convert to platform-native on checkout.
# Closes the 1,720-file CRLF mount-artifact noise that comes from the
# Windows host (CRLF on disk) vs git's LF-internal view. Without this,
# every file shows as modified in `git status` on the Linux workspace
# mount, even though no content has changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF even on Windows checkouts (bash + Docker
# CMD interpretation requires it).
*.bash text eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts on Windows are fine with CRLF; let git auto-detect.
*.ps1 text

# Binary types — never normalize.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
*.gz binary
*.7z binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary

# WINDOWS BATCH (2026-08-24). Ang `* text=auto eol=lf` sa itaas ay nagno-normalize
# ng LAHAT sa LF sa checkout. Para sa .cmd/.bat iyon ay panganib, hindi kagustuhan:
# ang `run-*-bridge.cmd` ay may supervisor restart loop na nakasalalay sa
# `:bridge_loop` / `goto bridge_loop`, at ang cmd.exe ay may kilalang
# label-resolution na kapritso sa mga LF-only na file. Ang buhay na gumaganang
# kopya ay CRLF (54 CRLF, 0 LF-lang) -- panatilihin iyon nang eksakto.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
